{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CfdbnzoM4N8jH8RdvNtkd","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I wrote `verdict.json` with an **upheld** verdict. I couldn't find a way to break any of the three checks.\n\n- **E05.1 holds.** Tools are keyed `${serverId}__${t.name}`. The `serverId` comes from the release manifest, which pins the endpoint and TLS certificate. `registerMcp` rejects any server id not in the manifest. The server's self-reported name is only logged. A later server can't overwrite an earlier entry, because `add()` rejects a duplicate key.\n- **E05.2 holds.** `add()` rejects the same bare name from another server. It also rejects lookalikes: `canonical()` normalizes case, homoglyphs and separators, then an edit-distance-1 check runs against every tool from other servers.\n- **E05.3 holds.** The reviewer's cited line (`config/policy.yaml:6`) only lists the tool as high-impact, so I traced the actual binding in `executor.ts` and `approvals.ts`. The executor uses `call.name`, which is the namespaced key. `checkApproval` requires `rec.tool === req.tool`, so a same-named tool from another server gets a different key and inherits no approval.\n\nI didn't run anything, only read the files. The sheet asks for `E05.verdict.json` or `verdicts.json`, but your instructions said to write only `verdict.json`, so I followed yours."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1127,"cache_read_input_tokens":18870,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1127},"output_tokens":456,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"ee1948c6-3a3b-4f3d-842d-cc25cb671314","uuid":"149f6216-556c-47f5-968a-1ed2d3036c41","timestamp":"2026-10-02T14:53:08.682Z","request_id":"